Build against this repository's whatsmeow pin.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, not upstream.

Why: meowcaller requires github.com/polymorfa/hypermeow, a whatsmeow fork with the
same packages. third_party/meowcaller.sh rewrites that import path to go.mau.fi/whatsmeow
(upstream's own #33 says the fork needs no code change), which leaves a require line
naming a fork pseudo-version whatsmeow does not have. This sets it to the pin in the
connector's go.mod and is the `go mod tidy` that follows. A whatsmeow bump in the
connector regenerates this patch.

